Reporting requirements:
The auditor must immediately report the following matters to the authority:
- losses have been incurred that reduce the capital of the Operator by at least 50%;
-irregularity that has or may have a material effect on the accounts of the Operator, including any irregularity that had caused a major disruption to the provision of any type of service to the customers of the Operator

Transparency & disclosure:
Entrepreneurs are prohibited from misleadingly offering, promoting
advertising certain goods and/or cervices if:
- the goods are not in good and/or new condition;
- the goods and/or services have obtained and/or had a sponsor, approval, certain features, certain advantages, certain workingcharacteristics or accession;
- using exaggerated words, such as safe, not harmful, not risky, no side effect without complete information,
-offering something containing unsecured promise.

Sanctions:
 Administrative sanction:
- administrative sanction can be imposed  to the entrepreneurs who violate entrepreneur's obligation
-The administrative sanction shall be determined in maximum
amount of Rp. 200, 000,000 (two hundred million rupiah).

Criminal charges:
Criminal charges can be filed against the entrepreneurs and/or theiradministrators.

Apart from the criminal penalty, additional penalties can also be imposed in the form of:
a. confiscation of certain goods;
b. announcement of judge’s decision;
c. payment for damages;
d. injunction to stop certain activities that cause damages to the consumers;
e. the obligation to pull out goods from circulation; or
f. revocation of business permit

Safeguarding of Funds:
Providers are required to have mechanisms and procedures
for the protection of Consumers’ assets, including maintaining the security of Consumers’ assets against misuse, including:
a. deception, leakage of information, and banking crimes (fraud);
b. scam; and
c. abuse and embezzlement of other assets (misuse)"

