-A MTO shall investigate each complaint received and shall respond to the customer in writing within ten (10) business days setting out a proposed remedy to the customer’s complaint

Consumer data protection & privacy:
Businesses, whether by themselves or by authorizing or hiring a third party to collect, store, use, modify, update, or cancel consumer information must ensure the safety and security of consumer information as stipulated by this Law and other relevant laws. In case businesses authorize or hire a third party to collect, store, use, modify, update or cancel consumer information, they must obtain the consumers’ consent

-Businesses must ensure the safety and security of consumer information
that they collect, store, or use, and take measures to prevent the following acts:
a) Unauthorized theft or access to information;
b) Unauthorized use of information;
c) Unauthorized modification, update or deletion of information
